                            "past"
                        ],
                        "form": "choreographed"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "8db83c35-2889-3fdb-964c-91867a8d1b57",
                        "entry_id": "337b3133-164c-32bd-957b-76d18cc6a0b2",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To design and record the choreography for a dramatic work such as a ballet."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "transitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ae3018a3-9203-4a68-b965-8c53e0335ab5",
                                "sense_id": "8db83c35-2889-3fdb-964c-91867a8d1b57",
                                "text": "So he choreographs each event depending on the crowd, starting with something to learn the drill, like “Marching Through Georgia,” working in something to loosen people up like the hokeypokey, and probably a contra dance (long lines, not squares) like the Virginia reel."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8e9355c5-22cd-4bb4-bae2-f722dbf886cb",
                                "sense_id": "8db83c35-2889-3fdb-964c-91867a8d1b57",
                                "text": "She and her two best friends are choreographing a number for the talent show; she’s applied to California Institute of the Arts; and she flirts unabashedly with a cute pizza server. (The better to land a couple of extra pepperonis on her slice without an upcharge.)"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "4ef244b9-e48b-3b31-9eac-6cf4ed27a4b5",
                        "entry_id": "337b3133-164c-32bd-957b-76d18cc6a0b2",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To direct the development of a project; to orchestrate."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "transitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "200291ce-212a-4770-9694-225787c7e3cc",
                                "sense_id": "4ef244b9-e48b-3b31-9eac-6cf4ed27a4b5",
                                "text": "Fight sequences fall into one of three categories: “MAMs” (many against many), “OHMs” (one hits many), and “triple O′s” (one on one). Group fights — MAMs and OHMs — are more difficult to choreograph than triple O′s, and TV shows that included well-choreographed MAMs and OHMs received higher marks than those devoid of mass attacks."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c4448db0-4ef3-4bec-b0c9-084a2c5bed68",
                                "sense_id": "4ef244b9-e48b-3b31-9eac-6cf4ed27a4b5",
                                "text": "England’s response came in the form of the brilliantly choreographed move that concluded with Wayne Rooney’s second goal and the kind of outstanding football that was beyond their opponents."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "0820f2b9-1cb9-3dec-9836-c3b77932c73d",
                        "entry_id": "337b3133-164c-32bd-957b-76d18cc6a0b2",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To work as a choreographer."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "intransitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    }
